Dependencies must be stable: If you create objects or arrays inside your component, they will be new references on every render. Either move them outside the component or memoize them. Don’t create functions inside useMemo: This can lead to unexpected behavior. scala // Don't do this val memoizedValue = useMemo(() => { val helper = () => doSomething() helper() }, Seq()) Empty dependencies array vs. null: With an empty array, the value is computed once. With null, it’s computed on every render. ```scala // Computed once val value1 = useMemo(() => expensive(), Seq())
// Computed on every render val value2 = useMemo(() => expensive(), null) ```
Infinite loops: Be careful not to create dependencies that change on every render. Non-serializable values: The dependency array should contain values that can be compared with ==.

